{"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"],"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa","text":"Vertices"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Vertices.Index == Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DirectedPseudograph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"code":"vertexIndex(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; on "},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, with no hashing, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" In addition to ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_key(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_vertex(atKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the members of the same name without the label, for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the vertex’s key is now ","type":"text"},{"code":"k","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; otherwise it returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and no other key changes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeEdge(at:)"},{"text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, trapping on any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)"},{"type":"text","text":", returning the removed instance."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key density.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":", plus O(1) per live vertex: the memory of the representation’s own page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span can exceed the vertex count: removals leave holes, and a decoded graph may start at any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position (its decoder bounds the span at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × vertexCount + 64"},{"type":"text","text":" pages). Keys before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest live key cost nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key rows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return the stored rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuccessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PredecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the elements are positions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not requirements.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" differs in its return type: ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple, returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new position, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. So generic code inserts an edge by key, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hooks are underscored because they are for wrappers inside the library: callers use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representations’ own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"type":"text","text":" members, which take vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L50","fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift"},"roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"title":"MutableDirectedGraph","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertices"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","required":true,"title":"Vertices"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols